title: 'chain-spec-builder: manage the boot nodes of a chain spec'
doc:
- audience: [Node Dev, Node Operator]
  description: |-
    `chain-spec-builder` can now manage the boot nodes of a chain specification. The new
    `add-bootnodes`, `remove-bootnodes`, `set-bootnodes` and `list-bootnodes` commands operate on
    an existing chain spec, in both plain and raw format, and the `create` command takes a new
    `--bootnodes` argument. The given addresses are validated: they must be multiaddresses
    containing the peer id of the node.
crates:
- name: staging-chain-spec-builder
  bump: minor
- name: sc-chain-spec
  bump: minor
